  "notes": [
    "carBox: measured on a 5x pixel ruler (tail x 59, nose x 338, roof y 488, tyres y 564). Set so the crop (box + 4% pad) ends exactly at the car: any looser crop let the segmenter take the blister bubble above the roof and the blister ends at nose and tail.",
    "wheels: measured on a 10x ruler; Hough found them 2-5 px too big and the front one 6 px too high.",
    "segModel: birefnet-general instead of the lite default; lite followed the blister bubble over the roof.",
    "model.rebake.glass: every view traced on the mesh (sheet glass from front/rear covered the whole roof header and lip, from the sides it took the roof and the A/C-pillar slopes); Tripo painted its glass tan on a black car, so `outline` (dark paint) found the body, and the polygons were traced by hand on tripo-sheet/tripo-clay zooms with a sheet-px ruler.",
    "model.rebake.glass.top: rear window (x 186-291), the two T-top panels inside their frames (x 371-512, y 757-862, mirrored; the centre roof bar and the roof section between the rear window and the T-tops with the sail-panel birds stay paint) and the windscreen (x 558-650). Traced on one half, glass_mirror.",
    "model.rebake.glass.front/rear: windscreen and rear window only, inside the chrome frame; the front one steps over the hood scoop (x 214-262 above y 1228) so the scoop is not glass. Mirrored left-right.",
    "model.rebake.glass.side/left: door window (an open window on the toy, the sheet draws it see-through; the mesh closes it, so it is glass to show the cabin), the T-top glass where it wraps down above the door window (x 363-523 / 501-659, stops at the chrome rail), and the edge-on slivers of rear window and windscreen behind/ahead of the pillars. Each side traced on its own view.",
    "No model.rebake.tinted: the toy's glass is light smoked/tan, not privacy-dark."
  ],
